<title>INDIA: India's ICICI sells hotel stock.</title>
<headline>India's ICICI sells hotel stock.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Industrial Credit and Investment Corporation of India (ICICI) said on Friday it has sold shares in Indo Continental Hotels &amp; Resorts Ltd through a negotiated sale.</p>
<p>The finance firm said it sold 88,634 shares which represented 5.91 percent of the hotel firm's capital at 90 rupees per share.</p>
<p>It did not give details.</p>
<p>--Bombay newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
